@startuml 05_-_whatsapp_mcp
title 05 - whatsapp mcp: opencode only, not part of the pipeline
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty members
component "opencode (Mac) - MCP stdio client, mcp.servers.whatsapp in opencode.json" as n0
component "whatsapp-mcp-server - Python, uv run main.py in tools/whatsapp-mcp" as n1
component "whatsapp-bridge - Go / whatsmeow, WhatsApp Web multi-device, QR link" as n2
component "SQLite store/messages.db - local history, chats + messages" as n3
component "personal WhatsApp account - paired device, the user controls the phone" as n4
component "MCP tools - search_contacts, list_messages, list_chats, get_chat, get_message_context" as n5
component "MCP tools - send_message, send_file, send_audio_message, download_media" as n6
component "scope note - opencode only, NOT wired into the campaign pipeline or k3s" as n7
n0 --> n1 : MCP stdio
n1 --> n2 : HTTP queries / sends
n2 --> n3 : persist
n2 --> n4 : multi-device protocol
n0 --> n5 : tools/list
n0 --> n6 : tools/call
n0 --> n7
note as guide
  opencode only: nothing in the campaign pipeline or the k3s cluster
  calls these tools.
  Install: brew install go, clone lharries/whatsapp-mcp under
  ~/ZCodeProject/tools, then go build the bridge.
  The bridge keeps WhatsApp Web multi-device state in a local SQLite
  store and prints a QR code to pair.
  Pairing needs the user's phone (WhatsApp > Linked devices); the
  re-link window is about 20 days.
  No message is sent by setup; sends happen only on an explicit ask.
end note

@enduml
